This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.

Summary:
1. Primary Request and Intent:
   This session continued from a previous context where a UBX-G7020-KT GPS module (u-blox M7, protocol v14.xx) was added to an M5Stack CoreS3 running bGeigieZen firmware. The GPS uses NMEA fallback mode (only GPS TX→GPIO18/RXD2 is wired; GPS RX←GPIO17/TXD2 is unconnected). Over this session the user requested:
   - Replace the verbose TX test hex-dump log with GPS module identification
   - Fix satellite display flickering
   - Fix: satellite text labels not centered in circles (from photo review)
   - Fix: status bar showing total visible satellites (12) instead of used-in-nav (5)
   - Fix: GPS shows GPS0 (orange) on boot until switching modes
   - Confirmed M8/M10 modules must continue working unchanged

2. Key Technical Concepts:
   - **NMEA fallback mode**: GPS TX→GPIO18 only; GpsConnector parses $GPRMC/$GPGGA/$GPGSV/$GPGSA in software
   - **nmea_gsv_cycle counter**: New field in GnssData, incremented when last GPGSV message of a sequence arrives, used to rate-limit NavsatCollector to once per complete GSV cycle
   - **M5Canvas sprite rendering**: Draws constellation map off-screen then pushes atomically — eliminates fillRect→draw flicker
